SUMMARY:Sep 12th An Evening of Spicy/Sensual Snuggles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your ticket-\nhttps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/sep-12th-an-evening-o
 f-sensual-snuggles\n\nWhat is a Sensual Snuggle Event?\\*\\*\nThis is a sw
 eet & welcoming event where we practice and use verbal consent to connect 
 and share touch. We talk about boundaries and practice both saying and rec
 eiving a “no”. In this space it is common to see people cuddle\, share
  massage\, have their hair brushed\, kiss\, expose nipples\, play\, laugh\
 , cry\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can relax and co
 nnect with other humans who are seeking touch based connection.\nWe strive
  for this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability to connect w
 ith and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are able to re
 lax\, feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\n**Our Agreements:**\n1- We ask 
 for what we want an wait for a yes before touching others.\n2- We say no i
 f we don’t want to do something.\n3- We try to receive a no with grace a
 nd not take it personally.\n4- We arrive on time\, clean (as scent free as
  possible)\, and sober.\n5- We keep our pants/shorts on at this event. (To
 ps are optional\; this is a sensual space\, not a sexual space.)\n6- We ar
 e here to connect with others. Connection can be verbal\, platonic\, or sp
 icy!\n7- We welcome diversity. Isms and Phobias are not welcome here!\n\n*
 *Who should attend:**\nPeople who are interested in safely exploring touch
  and sensuality with strangers. This includes people who are single\, peop
 le who are not single\, couples\, folks who are new to town and looking fo
 r connection\, people of all/any genders and sexual orientations\, people 
 of all ages (18 and up). People who understand and respect consent\, who w
 ill take care of themselves and people around them. This event is queer-no
 rmative. The guest list will include all genders\, orientations\, ages\, a
 nd personalities. If that’s not your thing… This is not the event for 
 you.\n***Who should NOT attend:***\n-People who are only looking for a sex
  party.\n-People who do not understand and respect consent.\n-People who h
 ave extreme fear of setting and speaking their personal boundaries\; in or
 der to create a safe space we need to know that you will say “no” if y
 ou feel a no.\n-People who are homophobic\, racist\, sexist\, ageist\, abl
 eist…\n-People under 18 years of age.\n***Schedule of the Evening***\n\n
 \\*6:50pm Doors Open\, Mix & Mingle\n\n* 7:00pm We gather in a circle to m
 eet each other\, build a container\, cover consent and boundary setting an
 d discuss event agreements. Then we will play a few intimacy building game
 s to meet and connect with other people in the room. Please make sure you 
 arrive on-time!\n\\*8:15pm Once the container is built we will have self d
 irected snuggling and sensual interactions until the end of the party.\n* 
 10:50pm Closing Circle\; a time to re-center and connect as a group to ver
 bally share anything that came up at the event or to voice gratitude to so
 meone(s) you enjoyed interacting with.\n\\*11:00pm cleanup & head home\; y
 ou are welcome to help.\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously
 !** If you experience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not 
 safe to be at this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doi
 ng our best to create a safe environment which means that if someone is ca
 using harm (physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this incl
 udes harm that takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivo
 rs and know that some of our participants are here to heal from touch base
 d trauma.\n\nThese events are not "gender balanced"[. Check out our websit
 e for more information about this decision.](http://holdmeavl.com/why-i-do
 nt-gender-balance-events/)\n\n**Simple definitions/clarifications-** Plato
 nic- marked by the absence of romance or sex.\nMost of the interactions we
  have with friends and strangers are platonic.\nSensual- gratification of 
 the senses or the indulgence of appetite.\nWe might feel sensual when we f
 eel someone's breath on our neck or experience a extra long and slow cares
 s.\nSexual- having or involving sex.\nOften involving one more more people
 s genitals\; perhaps seeking orgasm.\n\\*Refund Policy- Full refund if you
  cancel 7 days before the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergency\,
  or direct exposure to covid. Credit towards a future event if you cancel 
 more than 3 days before an event. No refund if you cancel within 2 days of
  the event or no-show.
