SUMMARY:Sep 13th Queer Platonic Cuddles 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\n**[REGISTER HERE](https://www.zef
 fy.com/en-US/ticketing/sep-13th-4-7pm-queer-platonic-cuddles-tranzmission-
 benefit)**[ ](https://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/sep-13th-4-7pm-queer-p
 latonic-cuddles-tranzmission-benefit)(rsvp's on Meetup do not count as reg
 istering)\nThis event is a fundraiser for Tranzmission. 100% of ticket sal
 es go directly to them!\n\nThis is an event for Adults who identify as LGB
 TQIA+.\nThe intention of this event is to build community and provide a su
 pportive place for participants to explore sweet platonic physical touch.\
 nNo one turned away for lack of funds (please ask if you truly need a scho
 larship or work trade).\n**This is a sweet & welcoming event where we prac
 tice and use verbal consent to connect and share touch.** We talk about bo
 undaries and practice both saying and receiving a “no”. In this space 
 it is common to see people cuddle\, share massage\, have their hair brushe
 d\, laugh\, cry\, and be vulnerable. This is a sober space where we can re
 lax and connect with other humans who are seeking touch based connection.\
 nWe strive for this to be a safe event. Safe touch enhances our ability to
  connect with and trust people. When we are in a space of safety\, we are 
 able to relax\, feel comfort\, and be vulnerable.\n\nConsent and respect a
 re at the forefront of the experience. We strive for a safe and welcoming 
 environment\, fostering a sense of trust that allows attendees to fully en
 joy shared touch without any pressure or expectations.\n\nDiscover the joy
  of shared vulnerability in an environment where your authenticity is not 
 just accepted but celebrated. This event is an opportunity to connect with
  like-minded individuals who appreciate the simplicity of human touch and 
 the profound impact it can have on our well-being.\n\nExpress yourself in 
 a way that feels true to you\, whether through cozy attire or a touch of p
 ersonal flair. We encourage individuality and self-expression\, creating a
 n inclusive space where everyone can be their authentic selves. Dress code
  is Casual and cozy.\n\nThis event will be indoors. Masks are optional. DO
  NOT ATTEND if you or someone you are physically close with is sick.\n\nTh
 is is an inclusive environment where we will aim to foster the dismantling
  of and no tolerance of ableism\, fat-shaming\, homophobia/transphobia\, s
 exism\, xenophobia\, classism\, racism & other ideas that lead to folks fe
 eling disconnected or unwelcome.\n\n**THE RULES**\n1\\. Pants stay on for 
 the whole event\\.\n2\\. You do not have to touch anyone at this event\\.\
 n3\\. You must ask permission and receive a verbal YES before you touch an
 yone\\. Please be specific in your requests\\.\n4\\. If you feel a yes\\\,
  say YES\\. If you feel a no\\\, say NO\\. If you’re a maybe\\\, say NO\
 \. You can always change your mind\\.\n5\\. Get your facilitator if you ha
 ve a question or concern\\\, or if you need assistance with anything durin
 g the event\\.\n6\\. Talking\\\, laughter\\\, silence\\\, silliness\\\, st
 illness\\\, and crying are welcome\\.\n\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n* ARRIVE ON TIME
 : It is important that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle.\
 n* Please be free of strong scents\; many folks would rather not be close 
 to someone who smells of perfume\, essential oils\, or cigarettes\n* BE SO
 BER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this event.\n\n**WHAT TO BR
 ING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share. The only thing that you 
 are required to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nWe take individual and 
 group safety seriously! if you experience\, see\, or know that one of our 
 participants is not safe to be at a touch based event we want to know abou
 t it. We are committed to doing our best to create a safe environment whic
 h means that if someone is causing harm (physical or mental) that person i
 s not welcome here (this includes harm that takes place outside of our eve
 nts). We stand behind survivors and know that some of our participants are
  here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\n\\*refund policy- Full refund if
  you cancel 7 days before the event or you cancel due to illness\, emergen
 cy\, or direct exposure to covid. Credit towards a future event if you can
 cel more than 3 days before an event. No refund if you cancel within 2 day
 s of the event or no-show.
