SUMMARY:Sep 18th Community Cuddles
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Cuddle Collective\nPlease note- If you want to atten
 d this event you need to purchase a ticket- We advertise in many places an
 d only paid tickets will reserve your space. use the link below to reserve
  your tickethttps://www.zeffy.com/en-US/ticketing/sep-18-community-cuddle\
 n\n**This is a non-sexual touch based event that invites participants to e
 xplore platonic intimacy in a safe environment** with like-minded people. 
 We respect personal boundaries and through a supportive framework of mutua
 l agreements that maximize safety and create a space of easy openness and 
 compassionate connection.\nAt this event we have the chance to normalize t
 ouch with clear boundaries\; this is a space for respectful\, consent-base
 d touch. We allow ourselves to be seen. We have fun.\nWe welcome people of
  all backgrounds\, genders\, ethnicities\, relationship styles\, sexualiti
 es\, sizes\, and ages (18+).\n\n**THE RULES**\n\n1. Clothes stay on for th
 e whole event.\n2. You do not have to touch anyone at this event.\n3. You 
 must receive a verbal YES before you touch anyone.\n4. Take care of yourse
 lf and those you choose to interact with.\n5. Speak up if you have a quest
 ion\, concern\, or if you need assistance with anything during the event.\
 n6. All emotions are welcome- we love vulnerability.\n**WHY CUDDLE?**\nTou
 ch is a basic human need\, and many of us do not get enough\; most people 
 don’t even know they are missing touch\, or have a way to ask for touch 
 without sexualizing it. We believe deeply in the power of touch\, and the 
 importance of communication and consent in creating a safe space for touch
 .\nCUDDLING WITH STRANGERS\nCuddling with strangers sounds weird or scary 
 to most people. “Will I like it?” “What if someone wants to touch me
  and I don’t want to?” “What if I say yes and it’s not what I want
 ?” “What if I really want to touch someone and they say no?” These a
 re all normal questions. The answer is that this is a space created to ask
  for exactly what you want\, and receive NOTHING you don’t want. Many pe
 ople start out nervous at a cuddle event & most are really glad they came.
 \n\n**Schedule:**\n6:50-7pm: Arrive with snacks to share! Get comfortable\
 , meet\, mingle\, & snack.\n7:05pm: Welcome Circle- its mandatory. We will
  set our container\, talk about personal boundaries\, communication\, & co
 nsent.\n7:15pm: Icebreakers and connective activities.\n8:00pm: Open cuddl
 ing! You MUST ask and get a verbal ‘yes’ before touching or cuddling w
 ith anybody at this event. If you are not sure how to do this – great! 
 – we will talk about it during the welcome circle.\n10:50pm: Closing Cir
 cle\, cleanup and head home.\n**ETIQUETTE**\n\n\\*ARRIVE ON TIME: It is im
 portant that all participants arrive before the Welcome Circle. The Welcom
 e Circle serves the purpose of creating the safe space for consensual\, no
 n-sexual touch between participants and making sure that everyone is infor
 med about consent.\n\n* Please arrive clean & as scent free as possible.\n
 \\*BE SOBER: Please do not drink or smoke before or at this event.\n\n**WH
 AT TO BRING:** personal water bottle and snacks to share\, a friend\, a da
 te – whatever cuddle accessories you like! The only thing that you are r
 equired to bring is a clean and sober you.\n\nThese events are not "gender
  balanced".\n\n**We take individual and group safety seriously!** If you e
 xperience\, see\, or know that one of our participants is not safe to be a
 t this event we want to know about it. We are committed to doing our best 
 to create a safe environment which means that if someone is causing harm (
 physical or mental) that person is not welcome here (this includes harm th
 at takes place outside of our events). We stand behind survivors and know 
 that some of our participants are here to heal from touch based trauma.\n\
 n\\*refund policy-\nFull refund if you cancel 7 days before the event or y
 ou cancel due to illness\, emergency\, or direct exposure to covid/flu.\nC
 redit towards a future event if you cancel more than 3 days before an even
 t.\nNo refund if you cancel within 2 days of the event or no-show.
